  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Lavajyoti Bora vs The State Of Assam And Anr on 10 February, 2020 Author: Kalyan Rai Surana Bench: Kalyan Rai Surana Page N Gahc010303122019 The Gauhati High Court (High Court Of Assam, Nagaland, Mizoram And Arunachal Pradesh) Case No. : Crl.Pet. 1472/2019 1:Lavajyoti Bora Asstt. General Manager (Pers And Admin), Food Corporation Of India, Regional Office, Guwahati-8, R/O Basisthapur Road No. 4, Beltola P.O., Guwahati-781028 Versus 1:The State Of Assam And Anr. Represented By The Public Prosecutor, Assam 2:Karuna Kt. Doley C/O Food Inspector (Senior) Joint Director Health Services Lakhimpur Lakhimpur And Dhemaji District Assa Advocate for the Petitioner : Mr B K Singh Advocate for the Respondent : Pp, Assam Before Honourable Mr. Justice Kalyan Rai Surana Order Date : 10.02.2020 Heard Mr. B.K. Singh,",
    "facts": "By referring to the documents annexed to this application and examination as well as the cross-examination of P.W.1 and P.W.2 recorded before framing of charge, it is submitted that there is no evidence before the learned trial Court that the petitioner was the nominated person under section 17(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 as regards FCI Godown at Japisajia, North Lakhimpur. It is submitted that as per the documents and evidence on record, one another person was the nominated vendor. Hence, it is submitted that the prosecution would not be maintainable.",
